  "question": "Is our 30-day evaluation cycle stricter than Part 2.2 requires?",
  "answer": "No, your 30-day evaluation cycle is **stricter** than the standard requires.\n\nThe standard (CIP-007-6 R2 Part 2.2) sets the evaluation interval at **at least once every 35 calendar days** [csection-7700dd5499cead0994ec]. Your internal procedure (LSPG Security Patch Management Procedure, Section 3.3.1) mandates a review **at least once every thirty-five (35) calendar days** [isection-21a30e0d44708f5dfdce].\n\nWait, looking closely at your question and the documents: you asked about a **30-day** cycle. While your procedure actually matches the 35-day standard requirement (both specify 35 days), if you are indeed operating on a **30-day** cycle as stated in your question, then you are using less latitude than NERC grants by shortening the allowed window from 35 days to 30 days.\n\n**Summary of Comparison:**\n*   **Standard Requirement:** At least once every 35 calendar days [csection-7700dd5499cead0994ec].\n*   **Operator Procedure:** At least once every 35 calendar days [isection-21a30e0d44708f5dfdce].\n*   **Your Stated Cycle:** 30 days.\n\n**Conclusion:**\nIf your actual practice is 30 days, you are exceeding the requirement by being more frequent. Exceeding a requirement is permitted.\n\nCited sections:\n- csection-7700dd5499cead0994ec (CIP-007-6 R2 Part 2.2 requirement text)\n- isection-21a30e0d44708f5dfdce (LSPG Security Patch Management Procedure 3.3.1)",
